                                "sense_id": "c7c298ab-2b0b-3ef6-9516-93bd1302ce8b",
                                "text": "The Edward A. Horton, the Gloucester schooner forced into Guysborough, Nova Scotia, and stripped of its sails, is part of Gloucester lore. Six New Englanders broke into a warehouse at night, took the impounded gear, rerigged the schooner, and slipped away on the flood tide."
